# Layer 1 (local, fast feedback) of the CI/Husky mandate for backend/API
# templates — hefesto's ADR 0014 §"CI/Husky mandatory", ADR 0026, and
# `.claude/rules/api-enforcement.md`'s enforcement-layer table ("1. Local —
# Husky pre-commit/pre-push in `create-coliapp` scaffolds — Fast feedback").
# Same shape as `templates/nextjs-kumo-console`'s own `.husky/pre-commit`:
# lint + format check, then type check. Kept fast and pre-commit-appropriate
# — no OpenAPI/license lint here (that's `.github/workflows/api-standard.yml`,
# PR-time) and no attestation gate (see `.husky/pre-push` for why that one
# can't run here).
#
# Deliberately excludes `pnpm test`: this template's own
# `scripts/__tests__/api-standard-gate.test.ts` includes two tests that
# assert against the `create-coliapp` monorepo's own root files (e.g.
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, two levels above `templates/express-ts`) and
# against real git history — both fail on a freshly scaffolded, standalone
# repo's first commit (no such root file exists there, and there is no prior
# HEAD to diff against yet). Running the full suite pre-commit would break
# the very first commit of every scaffold. Tracked as a separate, unfixed
# finding — not this hook's job to work around.
pnpm exec biome check . || exit 1
pnpm exec tsc --noEmit || exit 1

# OpenAPI generate-and-diff freshness (ADR 0040's 2026-08-31 addendum).
# Unlike `scripts/api-standard-gate.mjs` (`.husky/pre-push`), this reads the
# WORKING-TREE `openapi/openapi.yaml`, not a committed git blob — so, unlike
# that gate, it works correctly at pre-commit time and belongs here, not
# pre-push. Fast (sub-second): a small in-memory Zod→OpenAPI regeneration,
# no network, no git history walk.
pnpm run generate:openapi:check || exit 1
